    "result": "`encode` and `decode` are now implemented in `solution.py` to the spec. I wrote a 25-test suite in `tests/test_solution.py`, and `python -m pytest -q tests` passes all 25.\n\nThe tests cover these cases:\n- Run boundaries: runs of 3, 4, 5 and 12 characters, and runs made of `~`.\n- Round trips, including a non-ASCII character.\n- Lenient decoding of text `encode` would not produce, such as `~4~a~4~a`.\n- `ValueError` for malformed input: a trailing `~`, a leading zero, a count below 4, a count not followed by `~`, and a missing character after the count.",
